# CKA Lab Exercise: Fibre Channel (FC) SAN Storage Volume & Mount Drills

Hands-on training scenarios for the Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) exam covering enterprise Fibre Channel (FC)
SAN storage integration: direct in-tree Pod volume mounts, static PersistentVolumes and PersistentVolumeClaims with
`ReadWriteOnce`, raw block volume mounts (`volumeMode: Block`), dual-fabric multipathing, and SAN LUN expansion.

---

## 1. Overview & Architecture

The Fibre Channel SAN storage emulator provides an enterprise dual-fabric SAN environment across cluster nodes:

- **Target WWNN**: `20000025b5000001` (World Wide Node Name)
- **Fabric A Target WWPN**: `{{ cka_lab_fc_target_wwns[0] }}` (Primary Fabric Controller)
- **Fabric B Target WWPN**: `{{ cka_lab_fc_target_wwns[1] | default('5001438024266302') }}` (Secondary Controller for
  Multipath)
- **LUN 0**: 512 MiB volume &rarr; Filesystem target (`ext4`)
- **LUN 1**: 512 MiB volume &rarr; Raw block target (`volumeMode: Block`)
- **LUN 2**: 1024 MiB volume &rarr; Dynamic expansion and data recovery target

In Kubernetes, the in-tree `fc` volume plugin (`k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/volume/fc`) resolves device paths automatically
under
`/dev/disk/by-path/` matching `*-fc-0x${targetWWN}-lun-${lun}` or `/dev/disk/by-id/wwn-0x${wwid}`.

