## 5. Hands-on Drills

### Drill 1: Direct In-Tree Pod Volume Mount (`01-fc-direct-pod.yaml`)

Mounts LUN 0 directly in a pod spec without an intermediary PersistentVolume:

```bash
kubectl apply -f 01-fc-direct-pod.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/fc-direct-pod --timeout=120s
kubectl exec fc-direct-pod -- cat /mnt/storage/direct-test.txt
```

### Drill 2: Decoupled Static PV & PVC Filesystem Mount (`02-fc-pv-pvc-pod.yaml`)

Decouples storage administration (PV) from workload consumption (PVC):

```bash
kubectl apply -f 02-fc-pv-pvc-pod.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/fc-pvc-consumer-pod --timeout=120s
kubectl exec fc-pvc-consumer-pod -- df -h /mnt/storage
```

### Drill 3: Raw SAN Block Mode (`03-fc-raw-block.yaml`)

Exposes LUN 1 directly as a block device `/dev/fcblock` inside the container without a filesystem:

```bash
kubectl apply -f 03-fc-raw-block.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/fc-raw-block-consumer-pod --timeout=120s
kubectl exec fc-raw-block-consumer-pod -- ls -l /dev/fcblock
```

### Drill 4: Dual-Fabric Multipath PV (`04-fc-multipath-pv-pvc.yaml`)

Configures dual WWPN targets (`targetWWNs: ["5001438024266301", "5001438024266302"]`) representing redundant SAN
fabrics:

```bash
kubectl apply -f 04-fc-multipath-pv-pvc.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/fc-multipath-pod --timeout=120s
kubectl exec fc-multipath-pod -- df -h /mnt/storage
```

### Drill 5: Automated Verification Suite

Execute the comprehensive non-interactive verification script:

```bash
./test-fc-volumes.sh
```
